# Example specification: Inventory items

> Illustrative only. This is not a requirement for the application.
> Copy the [feature template](feature-template.md) for a real feature.

## Goal

Provide a REST API to manage inventory items and their categories.

## Data model

```mermaid
erDiagram
    CATEGORY ||--o{ ITEM : contains
    CATEGORY {
        int id PK
        string name
    }
    ITEM {
        int id PK
        string name
        int category_id FK
    }
```

In this example, names must be 1 to 100 characters long after trimming and
must not be blank.
Categories are pre-existing, every item belongs to exactly one category, and
item names need not be unique. Deleting a category with items is out of scope.

## API contract

All item responses contain `id`, `name` and `category_id`. Identifiers are
positive integers. The API does not require authentication in this example.

| Method and path | Behavior | Success |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `POST /items` | Create an item from `name` and `category_id` | 201 with item |
| `GET /items` | List all items, ordered by ascending ID | 200 with a JSON array |
| `GET /items/{item_id}` | Retrieve an item | 200 with item |
| `PUT /items/{item_id}` | Replace an item's name and category | 200 with item |
| `DELETE /items/{item_id}` | Delete an item | 204 with no body |

POST and PUT require both fields; unknown fields are rejected. Invalid input
returns 422. A missing item or category returns 404. Operations are persisted
in the application's database; create, update and delete are transactional.

## Acceptance criteria

- Creating an item in an existing category returns 201 and a subsequent GET
  returns the same data.
- Listing items returns an empty array when none exist and orders results by ID.
- Updating an item changes both fields; deleting it makes a subsequent GET
  return 404.
- An unknown item or category returns 404; an invalid name, ID, missing field
  or unexpected field returns 422.
- Tests cover each operation, invalid input and missing resources. Run those
  tests and `fastapi-harness check`, and report their actual results.
